id: temporal/calendars/0314
area: temporal
op: Temporal.PlainDate.from (property bag, options), calendar fields
in: str:"calendar" str:"ethiopic" str:"year" int:2015 str:"monthCode" str:"M00" str:"day" int:1 str:"overflow" str:"constrain"
out: error: RangeError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row C5: an invalid month code under constrain (M00, M13 where there is no thirteenth month, M14, M99) is constrained to the first or the last month in Coptic, Ethiopic, Indian, the Islamic calendars and Persian, where NonISOResolveFields throws a RangeError for a month code the calendar lacks (the milestone's listed correction); correction, answered by SJL-10.5
prov: proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-calendardatefromfields proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-parsemonthcode proposal:intl-era-monthcode@5833eae#sec-temporal-isvalidmonthcodeforcalendar ref:temporalref@1
script: (function (d) { return d.year + "/" + d.monthCode + "/" + d.day + ";" + d.month + ";" + d.toString({calendarName: "never"}); })(Temporal.PlainDate.from({calendar: "ethiopic", year: 2015, monthCode: "M00", day: 1}, {overflow: "constrain"}))
note: rows C4 and C5: month codes in each calendar's leap year under both overflows (the grammar's MonthCode, then Table 3's validity: an invalid code is a RangeError under constrain too)
since: 24

