out: error: RangeError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row C9: era names of earlier drafts and aliases the era proposal removed (gregory, gregory-inverse, coptic, hebrew, ethiopic, ethioaa, saka, persian, mundi, minguo, before-roc, incarnation) and ASCII case variants of the codes are accepted, where CanonicalizeEraInCalendar admits Table 2's codes and aliases only (decision D4); correction, answered by SJL-10.5
prov: proposal:intl-era-monthcode@5833eae#table-eras proposal:intl-era-monthcode@5833eae#sec-temporal-canonicalizeeraincalendar proposal:intl-era-monthcode@5833eae#sup-temporal-nonisoresolvefields proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-calendardatefromfields proposal:intl-era-monthcode@5833eae#sec-temporal-calendardateera overruled:temporalref@1=value:str:"roc;5;5;1916-01-01"
script: (function (d) { return d.era + ";" + d.eraYear + ";" + d.year + ";" + d.toString({calendarName: "never"}); })(Temporal.PlainDate.from({calendar: "roc", era: "minguo", eraYear: 5, monthCode: "M01", day: 1}))
note: rows C8 and C9: eras (Table 2's codes; the names of earlier drafts are refused) with eraYear 5; decision D7: the pinned text's answer, where its polyfill answers str:"roc;5;5;1916-01-01": Table 2 at the pinned era proposal lists no such era or alias for the calendar (the aliases mundi, minguo and before-roc left it on 2025-11-21, and incar and minguo-qian with them), so CanonicalizeEraInCalendar answers undefined and NonISOResolveFields throws a RangeError (decision D4)
since: 24

